WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.327
BEAR: A snow leopard.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.340
He hasn't eaten in days.

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:51.084
This may be his last chance.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:24.217
(theme music plays).

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm two miles
above sea level here,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.415
and it is brutal.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:02:00.820
Cold, desolate,
hard to breathe.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:05.792
But, for some, this is home.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.733
Mountains are one of the
most hostile environments

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:17.370
on our planet.

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:25.011
Now, with the rise in
global temperatures,

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.914
life is even tougher.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.852
The relentless
search for food.

00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:37.924
Intense competition.

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:42.695
Unpredictable weather.

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:03.616
Mountain animals are pushed
to the edge of existence.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:18.565
The Arctic Circle.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:24.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
Nowhere is the
planet warming faster.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:28.208
Spring has arrived here early.

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:36.048 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's bad news
for the barnacle geese

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:39.586
that breed in these mountains.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.992
Many nests have failed...

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:51.931
but not this one.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.403
Three chicks.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.506
They're lucky to have made it.

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:04.577
Forced by the early spring,

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.414
the parents rush
to their migration.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:12.718
They arrived exhausted.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:17.257 align:start size:81% position:19%
The female sat on
the eggs for 25 days.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.932
She's lost 30% of
her body weight.

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.338
But for this family,

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:35.575 align:start size:84% position:16%
the greatest challenge
is still to come.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:43.816
The parents chose to nest
on this 400 foot pinnacle.

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:51.057
It's the only way
to evade predators.

00:04:56.595 --> 00:05:00.033
Just one problem...

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.735 align:start size:78% position:22%
the grass they
eat is a mile away,

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.504
by the river.

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
And barnacle geese can't
feed their young in the nest.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.915
If the chicks don't
feed within 36 hours,

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:18.985
they'll starve.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:24.457 align:start size:97% position:3%
And these chicks won't be
able to fly for another month.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:31.531 align:start size:91% position:9%
The parents are living
proof there is a solution.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.569
Just not an easy one.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:52.652
Dad leads the way.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:02.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the chicks are
instinctively bonded to mum.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:14.073
Where she goes they follow.

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:10.062
(peeping).

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:14.066
Incredibly, it survived.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:19.705
But it's stunned.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:23.643
And now dangerously exposed.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:54.207
(honking, cawing).

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:08.387
One chick gone.

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:11.791 align:start size:78% position:22%
Now hope rests
with the other two.

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:22.134 align:start size:88% position:13%
The back of the
spire is a shorter drop.

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:29.742
But it's much harder
to avoid the rocks.

00:08:37.683 --> 00:08:42.054 align:start size:88% position:13%
For this chick,
there will be no escape.

00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:50.296
The third and last
surviving chick.

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:30.036
♪ ♪

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:07.073 align:start size:91% position:9%
The snow cushions the
impact, but offers no grip.

00:10:19.085 --> 00:10:25.725
(honking).

00:10:52.251 --> 00:10:56.355
Only around 50% of chicks
hatched on these cliffs

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:59.892
make it through the first month.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:07.433 align:start size:91% position:9%
With the seasons
increasingly unpredictable,

00:11:07.733 --> 00:11:11.671
fewer chicks will survive.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:20.146 align:start size:91% position:9%
But this chick, at
least, has defied the odds.

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:29.355 align:start size:91% position:9%
A changing climate is
affecting life in mountains

00:11:29.455 --> 00:11:32.391
across the world.

00:11:38.664 --> 00:11:40.966
Late winter.

00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:45.271
The average temperature here is
rising a degree every decade.

00:11:56.048 --> 00:11:59.151
Bad news for a snow leopard.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.289
Thick fur enables him to
withstand temperatures

00:12:04.389 --> 00:12:07.426
of -20 Fahrenheit.

00:12:12.697 --> 00:12:16.268
But today, it's 66.

00:12:18.069 --> 00:12:21.273
To find enough food, he
must patrol a territory

00:12:21.373 --> 00:12:24.777
of 80 square miles.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:33.886 align:start size:88% position:13%
Dry barren slopes
don't support much prey.

00:12:41.393 --> 00:12:44.864
It can be more than a
week between meals.

00:12:55.006 --> 00:12:57.510
He must make a kill,

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:04.483
or starve.

00:13:14.959 --> 00:13:18.264 align:start size:81% position:19%
BEAR: 16,000 feet
up in the Himalayas,

00:13:19.164 --> 00:13:22.067 align:start size:81% position:19%
a desperately
hungry snow leopard.

00:13:24.536 --> 00:13:28.440
His best opportunity in
days is within sight.

00:13:30.342 --> 00:13:33.144
Blue sheep.

00:13:33.612 --> 00:13:37.082
In this heat, he
can't run far.

00:13:38.483 --> 00:13:41.353
He needs to close the gap.

00:14:00.973 --> 00:14:05.176
His camouflage helps.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:10.316 align:start size:97% position:3%
But with so little cover,
it's hard to get close enough.

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:26.631
He ran too early.

00:14:26.731 --> 00:14:30.469
And it's too hot
to give chase.

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:34.339
Like all who live here,

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:38.344
his fortunes are linked
to the mountain climate.

00:14:40.612 --> 00:14:44.383
And even small changes can
have dramatic consequences.

00:15:00.799 --> 00:15:03.368 align:start size:78% position:22%
Here in Africa,
rising temperatures

00:15:03.468 --> 00:15:07.139 align:start size:81% position:19%
are forcing mountain
life ever higher.

00:15:16.982 --> 00:15:21.086 align:start size:81% position:19%
An army of Gelada
monkeys is gathering.

00:15:27.759 --> 00:15:31.063
They're all after one thing.

00:15:32.331 --> 00:15:36.635
But to find it, they must
climb higher and higher.

00:15:41.073 --> 00:15:44.609 align:start size:81% position:19%
Their numbers
grow to 1200 strong.

00:15:45.243 --> 00:15:49.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the largest gatherings
of monkeys on the planet.

00:15:56.655 --> 00:16:01.560
At 10,000 feet, this
is what they're after.

00:16:03.895 --> 00:16:05.464
Grass.

00:16:05.564 --> 00:16:08.500
It's almost all they eat.

00:16:11.603 --> 00:16:15.641
But so many monkeys in such
a small area means trouble.

00:16:24.115 --> 00:16:27.419
Especially for this old male.

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:36.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
He needs a lot of
energy to defend his family.

00:16:37.896 --> 00:16:42.034
Ten females and 12 youngsters.

00:16:47.205 --> 00:16:50.075
But you don't get
much from grass.

00:16:50.175 --> 00:16:53.479
He has to spend ten
hours a day feeding.

00:16:58.783 --> 00:17:03.455
And today he's gonna need
all the energy he can get.

00:17:10.162 --> 00:17:12.831
Bachelor males.

00:17:12.931 --> 00:17:14.666
Outcasts.

00:17:14.766 --> 00:17:17.770
Forced to the edge of society.

00:17:21.873 --> 00:17:26.077
Any one of them would be happy
to take down the old male and

00:17:26.177 --> 00:17:29.481
become the new family leader.

00:17:40.425 --> 00:17:44.596
To hold onto power, the old
male must prove his strength,

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:49.168 align:start size:81% position:19%
both to the bachelors
and his females.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:59.778 align:start size:78% position:22%
He challenges
them to chase him.

00:18:07.986 --> 00:18:14.259
(barking, yelling).

00:18:17.329 --> 00:18:20.432
But no one dares to attack.

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:24.203
His show of force has worked.

00:18:25.871 --> 00:18:28.774
For now.

00:18:31.009 --> 00:18:33.311 align:start size:81% position:19%
The old male has
little time to refuel

00:18:33.411 --> 00:18:36.715
before the herd moves on.

00:18:46.758 --> 00:18:49.661
The bachelors are back.

00:18:52.363 --> 00:18:56.168
(barking, yelling).

00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:00.205
At this high altitude,

00:19:00.305 --> 00:19:03.342
each confrontation
takes more energy.

00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:10.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
A relentless cycle of moving,
feeding and fighting.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:20.292
Moving, feeding, fighting.

00:19:23.695 --> 00:19:28.333
By late afternoon, the
old male is exhausted.

00:19:43.916 --> 00:19:47.685
The strongest bachelor,
45 pounds of muscle,

00:19:47.785 --> 00:19:50.923
with energy to burn.

00:20:06.504 --> 00:20:09.441 align:start size:84% position:16%
He's the most
serious challenger yet,

00:20:10.075 --> 00:20:12.611
and the old male knows it.

00:20:21.453 --> 00:20:24.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
BEAR: Two male Gelada
monkeys fight for supremacy.

00:20:26.458 --> 00:20:29.628
A dominant male and
a younger bachelor.

00:20:33.398 --> 00:20:37.569
One against one the
bachelor is stronger.

00:20:46.544 --> 00:20:49.681
The old male won't
last much longer.

00:20:52.283 --> 00:20:55.921
At least not alone.

00:20:57.489 --> 00:20:59.691
His females are loyal.

00:20:59.791 --> 00:21:03.262
They won't give up on
their protector yet.

00:21:09.401 --> 00:21:13.038
This united force
is overwhelming.

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:26.051
The old male is victorious.

00:21:27.251 --> 00:21:29.655
But it's tough at the top.

00:21:38.029 --> 00:21:42.200 align:start size:88% position:13%
As the climate warms and
the grass they depend
on retreats higher,

00:21:42.668 --> 00:21:46.438 align:start size:88% position:13%
their battle for survival
will only intensify.

00:22:03.088 --> 00:22:06.458 align:start size:91% position:9%
In the heat of mid-summer,
mountain goats seek out

00:22:06.558 --> 00:22:09.928
cooler temperatures
on the high ridges.

00:22:14.365 --> 00:22:18.369 align:start size:81% position:19%
This female is a
natural mountaineer.

00:22:18.903 --> 00:22:22.407 align:start size:88% position:13%
She can easily
access the best grazing,

00:22:22.507 --> 00:22:25.444
even with a kid in tow.

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:30.815
But there's one thing
they both need that's

00:22:30.915 --> 00:22:33.919
far harder to reach.

00:22:36.355 --> 00:22:38.623
Today, they must leave
the ridge and descend

00:22:38.723 --> 00:22:41.760
into the heat of the valley.

00:22:45.797 --> 00:22:50.035
For the little one, this
is a dangerous journey.

00:22:52.504 --> 00:22:55.740
With the mercury hitting
100 degrees Fahrenheit,

00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:59.444
this is the hottest
summer on record.

00:23:04.515 --> 00:23:06.651
After a winter of heavy snow,

00:23:06.751 --> 00:23:09.955 align:start size:81% position:19%
this means more
meltwater than ever.

00:23:17.662 --> 00:23:20.932
Mum's made this
journey before,

00:23:21.332 --> 00:23:25.704
but some rivers are at their
highest level in 100 years.

00:23:55.300 --> 00:24:01.840
♪ ♪

00:24:11.149 --> 00:24:13.518
Their goal is in sight.

00:24:13.618 --> 00:24:16.922
Just one more river to cross.

00:24:17.822 --> 00:24:21.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it's the
deepest and widest yet.

00:24:42.513 --> 00:24:45.684 align:start size:84% position:16%
The current is too
strong for little legs.

00:25:20.218 --> 00:25:24.089
And this is what they've
risked their lives for.

00:25:25.623 --> 00:25:29.260
A salt lick.

00:25:30.261 --> 00:25:34.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
These goats crave sodium,
an essential mineral lacking

00:25:34.365 --> 00:25:36.868
in their mountain diet.

00:25:44.576 --> 00:25:48.146 align:start size:78% position:22%
Summer in the
mountains is short.

00:25:49.180 --> 00:25:52.651
Harder times are coming.

00:26:02.127 --> 00:26:04.262
Temperatures plummet.

00:26:07.298 --> 00:26:09.668
Days shorten.

00:26:12.504 --> 00:26:15.040
Winter is here.

00:26:21.546 --> 00:26:24.816
But the hunt for
food must continue.

00:26:34.392 --> 00:26:38.196 align:start size:91% position:9%
Heavy snow on higher ridges
has forced these ibex

00:26:38.296 --> 00:26:41.199
down into the valley.

00:26:48.105 --> 00:26:50.108
A cold winter can
be a blessing for

00:26:50.208 --> 00:26:53.144
a hungry snow leopard.

00:26:55.880 --> 00:26:59.050
He's less likely to overheat.

00:27:02.820 --> 00:27:06.291
But against the white,
he's visible for miles.

00:27:14.933 --> 00:27:18.637
He must rely on stealth.

00:27:21.339 --> 00:27:24.342
Not easy in such deep snow.

00:27:39.424 --> 00:27:45.864
♪ ♪

00:28:09.520 --> 00:28:12.123
The distance was too great.

00:28:12.223 --> 00:28:15.260
The ibex too fast.

00:28:17.895 --> 00:28:21.832 align:start size:91% position:9%
Now all the animals in
the valley know he's here.

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:26.371
And he's burnt
precious energy.

00:28:30.407 --> 00:28:33.143
These are desperate times.

00:28:33.611 --> 00:28:35.713
If he's to see winter through,

00:28:35.813 --> 00:28:39.050 align:start size:78% position:22%
he may have to
take bigger risks.

00:28:45.923 --> 00:28:48.593
Throughout the mountains
of the Northern Hemisphere,

00:28:48.693 --> 00:28:51.730
winter's grip is tightening.

00:28:54.265 --> 00:28:57.835
Animals must make the most of
any last opportunity before

00:28:57.935 --> 00:29:01.873 align:start size:81% position:19%
conditions drive
them to take shelter.

00:29:05.342 --> 00:29:09.180
Far above, planetary forces
are on a collision course.

00:29:11.015 --> 00:29:13.484
A river of air,
the jet stream,

00:29:13.584 --> 00:29:16.821
flows around the North Pole.

00:29:16.921 --> 00:29:21.793 align:start size:88% position:13%
At its center, sits a
mass of cold Arctic air.

00:29:23.495 --> 00:29:27.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
But now a warming
upper atmosphere is
slowing the jet stream.

00:29:27.899 --> 00:29:31.536
And the cold air can escape.

00:29:36.174 --> 00:29:38.542
By the time it
hits The Rockies,

00:29:38.642 --> 00:29:42.113
it's grown into a mega storm.

00:29:42.747 --> 00:29:45.784 align:start size:84% position:16%
Freezing
everything in its path.

00:29:56.027 --> 00:29:59.263 align:start size:97% position:3%
BEAR: In the depths of winter,
extreme storms rage across

00:29:59.363 --> 00:30:02.033
Canada and the USA.

00:30:02.700 --> 00:30:04.335
Freezing temperatures,

00:30:04.435 --> 00:30:08.106
wind speeds of up to
150 miles per hour.

00:30:09.573 --> 00:30:13.845
Now, even the toughest animals
are at their limit of survival.

00:30:17.348 --> 00:30:23.988
(wind whistling).

00:30:38.202 --> 00:30:41.806
The storms may have passed,
but there is hidden danger

00:30:41.906 --> 00:30:44.542
in this landscape.

00:30:53.684 --> 00:30:57.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
Winter storms have buried
this area of British Columbia

00:30:57.588 --> 00:31:01.226
under nearly 40 feet of snow.

00:31:02.560 --> 00:31:06.163
But if temperatures
rise above freezing,

00:31:06.864 --> 00:31:09.901
it can have lethal consequences.

00:31:24.916 --> 00:31:28.085
On the high ridges, wind
driven snow has created

00:31:28.185 --> 00:31:32.423 align:start size:78% position:22%
huge overhangs,
some 25 feet thick.

00:31:37.962 --> 00:31:41.065 align:start size:91% position:9%
The longer the temperatures
stay above freezing,

00:31:41.165 --> 00:31:44.636 align:start size:78% position:22%
the more the
snow pack weakens.

00:31:59.850 --> 00:32:06.424
(crashing).

00:32:40.791 --> 00:32:44.595
Soon, tens of thousands of
tons of snow are traveling

00:32:44.695 --> 00:32:47.999
up to 80 miles an hour.

00:32:56.941 --> 00:33:00.577
As weather patterns change,
avalanches across the world

00:33:00.677 --> 00:33:03.348
are growing bigger.

00:33:41.385 --> 00:33:44.989
The more erratic and severe
mountain winters become,

00:33:45.089 --> 00:33:49.060
the more victims
they'll claim.

00:33:58.903 --> 00:34:02.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
But some are still succeeding
in this harsh world.

00:34:07.545 --> 00:34:11.582
Golden eagles live in almost
every mountain range in the

00:34:11.682 --> 00:34:14.385
Northern Hemisphere.

00:34:33.103 --> 00:34:36.874
They endure the alpine winter
by using the brutal conditions

00:34:36.974 --> 00:34:39.844
to their advantage.

00:34:47.318 --> 00:34:51.455
Like all golden eagles, this
female has a special sensory

00:34:51.555 --> 00:34:55.225 align:start size:84% position:16%
organ that detects
change in air pressure,

00:34:55.826 --> 00:34:59.564
allowing her to locate air
currents rising off ridges.

00:35:04.969 --> 00:35:10.274 align:start size:84% position:16%
With her seven foot
wingspan, she can climb
to over 11,000 feet.

00:35:14.411 --> 00:35:20.251
Then, to get to the next peak,
she folds her wings and dives.

00:35:35.833 --> 00:35:39.737
With a top speed of
150 miles per hour,

00:35:39.837 --> 00:35:43.608
she's one of the fastest
animals on the planet.

00:35:53.651 --> 00:35:57.755
It looks effortless,
and it needs to be.

00:36:01.225 --> 00:36:04.795
A golden eagle may cover
100 miles a day scouring

00:36:04.895 --> 00:36:08.466
the slopes for any opportunity.

00:36:21.111 --> 00:36:24.615
A flock of ravens
is a good sign.

00:36:28.519 --> 00:36:32.957
(cawing).

00:36:38.663 --> 00:36:41.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
During winter, golden eagles
are forced to scavenge

00:36:41.832 --> 00:36:44.468
90% of their food.

00:36:55.613 --> 00:37:01.552
If finding food is hard,
keeping it is even harder.

00:37:17.768 --> 00:37:21.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
A carcass like this
attracts a lot of attention.

00:37:48.999 --> 00:37:52.536
This male is powerful.

00:37:53.103 --> 00:37:56.040
And eagles don't share.

00:38:10.521 --> 00:38:13.257
Another brutal storm.

00:38:13.357 --> 00:38:16.827
This could be the last
chance to feed for days.

00:38:18.295 --> 00:38:20.998
Starvation is a
serious threat.

00:38:21.098 --> 00:38:24.769
Only a quarter of young eagles
will survive to reach maturity.

00:38:26.070 --> 00:38:29.540
Will it be him or her?

00:38:42.886 --> 00:38:46.991
Attacking from the air
gives her the advantage.

00:39:04.441 --> 00:39:07.845
But her victory
is short lived.

00:39:13.718 --> 00:39:17.455
Now both eagles may be
fighting for their lives.

00:39:24.628 --> 00:39:27.531 line:0%
BEAR: In the peaks of Norway,
two golden eagles are fighting

00:39:27.631 --> 00:39:29.934
for a chance to feed.

00:39:32.602 --> 00:39:35.740
Both are desperate.

00:39:42.245 --> 00:39:45.383
The female stands her ground.

00:39:48.218 --> 00:39:51.856
But the male is not done.

00:39:52.523 --> 00:39:59.096
(screaming).

00:40:10.574 --> 00:40:13.744
Each eagle is armed
with two inch talons.

00:40:14.611 --> 00:40:17.681
These fights can be deadly.

00:40:30.194 --> 00:40:33.197
Her kick was decisive.

00:40:35.632 --> 00:40:38.268
What's left of the frozen
flesh may be just enough

00:40:38.368 --> 00:40:41.572
to keep her alive.

00:40:47.845 --> 00:40:52.716
But this harsh winter
will drive others to
even greater extremes.

00:41:12.436 --> 00:41:17.174 align:start size:97% position:3%
This snow leopard's relentless
search for food continues.

00:41:23.180 --> 00:41:26.316
Following the scent
of prey has drawn him

00:41:26.416 --> 00:41:29.119
to the edge of his territory,

00:41:33.457 --> 00:41:36.827
and into a steep ravine.

00:41:45.435 --> 00:41:48.138
Blue sheep.

00:41:55.011 --> 00:41:58.782 align:start size:81% position:19%
The broken rock
provides good cover.

00:42:03.587 --> 00:42:08.058
But this is difficult terrain.

00:42:33.350 --> 00:42:38.756
Now, he must let
them come to him.

00:43:18.328 --> 00:43:24.735
♪ ♪

00:43:54.097 --> 00:43:58.769
A 200 foot fall,
never letting go.

00:44:12.349 --> 00:44:16.754 align:start size:88% position:13%
Finally, the snow
leopard can eat his fill.

00:44:31.568 --> 00:44:35.439 align:start size:78% position:22%
But success has
come at huge cost.

00:44:41.778 --> 00:44:44.448
He's badly injured.

00:44:49.653 --> 00:44:53.623 align:start size:81% position:19%
For a hunter that
lives by its agility,

00:44:53.723 --> 00:44:56.927
this could be fatal.

00:45:12.275 --> 00:45:16.246
The challenges of survival up
here at altitude is so extreme

00:45:16.346 --> 00:45:20.884
that it seems near impossible
that anything can make it.

00:45:20.984 --> 00:45:26.256 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the resilience of mountain
animals is near miraculous.

00:45:34.631 --> 00:45:38.936
Incredibly, just
three days later,

00:45:41.905 --> 00:45:46.443
we filmed the same snow
leopard back on its feet

00:45:46.943 --> 00:45:49.947
hunting again.

00:45:54.250 --> 00:45:57.354 align:start size:91% position:9%
It takes true grit to
survive in these desolate,

00:45:57.454 --> 00:45:59.356
unforgiving landscapes.

00:45:59.456 --> 00:46:02.926 align:start size:88% position:13%
But, somehow animals
still manage to triumph,

00:46:03.026 --> 00:46:06.730
to find shelter,
food and, perhaps,

00:46:06.830 --> 00:46:10.400
most importantly, each other.

00:46:20.043 --> 00:46:23.247 align:start size:91% position:9%
Against all odds, snow
leopards are still breeding

00:46:23.347 --> 00:46:26.450
here in the Himalayas.

00:46:28.485 --> 00:46:31.721
They are living proof of
mountain animals amazing

00:46:31.821 --> 00:46:35.259
ability to succeed
in a changing world.

00:46:42.232 --> 00:46:46.036 line:0%
Their offspring will be
the hope for the future.

00:47:04.054 --> 00:47:05.322 line:0%
Captioned by Cotter
Captioning Services.

